0-1.jpg?fit=crop&w=3200 3200w","https://www.datocms-assets.com/133654/1736518088-c-level-shoe-district-3-2048x1280-1.jpg?fit=crop&w=3200",1779,{"_modelApiKey":128,"title":129,"sideCopy":130,"mainCopy":131},"module_title_copy","'LUXURY'","\u003Cp>\u003Cspan data-metadata=\"&lt;!--(figmeta)eyJmaWxlS2V5IjoiWGJVSFVxeUc3bjVjOHRLZjg4NzJVdyIsInBhc3RlSUQiOjE5NTg3MzQzODUsImRhdGFUeXBlIjoic2NlbmUifQo=(/figmeta)--&gt;\" style=\"caret-color: #000000; color: #000000; font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: auto; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: auto; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration: none;\">\u003C/span>\u003Cspan>The Luxury category drew on a hyper elegance in form and finish. A one stop shop for occasion, wedding and work shoes.\u003C/span>\u003C/p>","\u003Cp>\u003Cspan>The approach was to marry products to place. It was imperative for the shopper to intuitively move towards &lsquo;their&rsquo; product choice via a series of &lsquo;pavilion&rsquo; based environments which anchored the shopper. The Luxury pavilion led the way.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan>\u003Cbr />\u003C/span>\u003C/p>",{"_modelApiKey":133,"assetPosition":134,"isWide":9,"assets":135},"module_framed_asset","center",[136,149,158],{"copy":31,"asset":137},{"isVideo":9,"videoHeight":30,"videoUrl":31,"videoWidth":32,"image":138},{"width":139,"height":140,"url":141,"alt":7,"title":7,"responsiveImage":142},870,1025,"https://www.datocms-assets.com/133654/1736518435-shed_lsd_130121_6156-1.jpg",{"webpSrcSet":143,"srcSet":144,"src":145,"width":146,"height":147,"sizes":148},"https://www.datocms-assets.com/133654/1736518435-shed_lsd_130121_6156-1.jpg?dpr=0.25&fit=crop&fm=webp&w=1740 435w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/133654/1736518435-shed_lsd_130121_6156-1.jpg?dpr=0.5&fit=crop&fm=webp&w=1740 870w,https://www.datocms-assets.com/133654/1736518435-shed_lsd_130121_6156-1.jpg?fit=crop&fm=w